Description: Ignore events for stopped sources.
 A timeout handler could stop a source after epoll_wait() reported it but
 before its event was dispatched; dispatch then ran FIONREAD on the closed
 fd, took it for a disconnect and aborted on an assert. Reachable at quit
 when the splash's idle timeout closes the terminal as getty hangs up the
 same VT.
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/plymouth/plymouth/-/commit/11a90cd3a8a6316f50993203127c39a3160c63d9
Applied-Upstream: 11a90cd3
Last-Update: 2026-10-10

--- a/src/libply/ply-event-loop.c
+++ b/src/libply/ply-event-loop.c
@@ -1259,6 +1259,16 @@
                 bool is_disconnected;
 
                 source = (ply_event_source_t *) (events[i].data.ptr);
+
+                /* A timeout handler can stop a source after epoll_wait ()
+                 * reports it but before its event is dispatched.
+                 */
+                if (!source->is_getting_polled) {
+                        if (loop->should_exit)
+                                break;
+                        continue;
+                }
+
                 status = ply_event_loop_get_fd_status_from_poll_mask (events[i].events);
 
                 is_disconnected = false;
